{"term":"dar uma de safado","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"horndog","concept":"horndog","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To act like a horndog or sexually forward person; to perform a flirtatiously lewd, naughty persona in social interaction.","english_term":"to act like a perv / to play the horndog","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Safado' means sexually naughty, shameless, or dirty-minded; 'dar uma de' means to put on the persona of. Used playfully or self-deprecatingly, rarely purely pejorative."}
{"term":"catfish sexual","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"catfishing","concept":"online_identity_deception","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":28,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":68,"recognition_pct_peak":68,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual catfishing; creating or using a false online identity to deceive someone into a romantic or sexual relationship.","english_term":"sexual catfishing","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Catfish' is borrowed directly from English internet slang; the compound 'catfish sexual' adds the explicit sexual motivation to distinguish it from non-romantic identity fraud."}
{"term":"assédio digital","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"internet_subculture","subcategory":"harassment","concept":"sexual_harasser_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":22,"technical":38,"recognition_pct_current":87,"recognition_pct_peak":87,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Digital sexual harassment; a pattern of unwanted sexual attention, messages, explicit images, or coercive advances conducted via online platforms or messaging apps.","english_term":"digital sexual harassment","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Assédio' means harassment; the registry concept is person-focused while this term names the act or pattern of behavior. Usage has risen sharply alongside #MeToo-adjacent discourse in Brazil since 2017."}
{"term":"ficar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To hook up with someone in a non-committed encounter, typically involving kissing and making out and sometimes more; the foundational verb of Brazilian casual-dating culture.","english_term":"to hook up / to make out","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to stay/remain' but the sexual usage is ubiquitous. The defining feature is absence of romantic commitment, not the specific physical act, which can range from a kiss to full sex depending on context."}
{"term":"ficada","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":18,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A hookup session; a single instance of ficando — a non-committed romantic-sexual encounter typically spanning kissing to light sexual activity.","english_term":"a hookup / a makeout session","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Noun form of 'ficar.' 'Tivemos uma ficada' = 'we hooked up once.' Carries no implication of a continuing relationship. Less crude in feel than the English 'hookup.'"}
{"term":"ficante","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup_partner","concept":"friends_with_benefits","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":18,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":94,"recognition_pct_peak":94,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A non-committed hookup partner; someone one makes out with or hooks up with regularly but without romantic commitment or exclusivity.","english_term":"hookup buddy / friends with benefits","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Not necessarily a friend first, unlike the FWB connotation. The relationship is defined by mutual ficadas with no strings. More explicitly non-committal than most FWB framings in English."}
{"term":"ficante sem compromisso","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"nsa_arrangement","concept":"casual_sex_arrangement","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":18,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A hookup partner with explicitly negotiated zero commitment; a ficante arrangement where both parties have verbally confirmed the no-strings-attached terms.","english_term":"no-strings-attached hookup partner / NSA arrangement","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Sem compromisso' = 'without commitment,' a phrase that recurs across many Brazilian social contexts. The redundancy over plain 'ficante' signals that at least one party wanted to formally foreclose expectations."}
{"term":"ficou com","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Past-tense idiom meaning someone hooked up with another person; the standard way to report a completed ficar encounter.","english_term":"hooked up with","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Ela ficou com o João na festa' = 'She hooked up with João at the party.' The phrase is so ubiquitous it functions almost as a grammatical construction rather than slang."}
{"term":"arranjou alguém","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":10,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Succeeded in finding a romantic or sexual partner for the night; 'got with someone' at a social event.","english_term":"got with someone / scored","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'arranged/found someone.' Very mild in register; emphasizes the social outcome of finding a partner over any physical act. Context determines whether this implies a kiss, a full hookup, or just someone's phone number."}
{"term":"pegação","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup_culture","concept":"hookup_culture","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":30,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The act, practice, or ambient culture of casual hookups and making out; the general pursuit of non-committed physical encounters at parties or social events.","english_term":"hookup culture / the making-out scene","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Nominalization of 'pegar.' 'Muita pegação nessa festa' = 'lots of hooking up at this party.' Can name one event's atmosphere or the broader Brazilian social phenomenon. Slightly more physically charged in connotation than the ficar family."}
{"term":"pegar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To hook up with someone; to make out with or have sexual contact with a person, typically in a casual, non-committed encounter.","english_term":"to hook up with / to pull","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to catch/grab.' More assertive in physical connotation than 'ficar'; can cover a kiss through full sex depending on context. 'Consegui pegar ela' = 'I managed to hook up with her.' One of the most versatile sexual slang verbs in Brazilian Portuguese."}
{"term":"rodar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"hookup_failure","concept":"hookup","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":83,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To fail to hook up at a party or social event; to strike out and go home without a partner after attempting pegação.","english_term":"to strike out / to go home empty-handed","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to spin/rotate,' evoking the image of circling the venue all night without success. Opposite of 'pegar' in outcome. No registry concept covers this failure-to-hookup meaning specifically; concept slug denotes the same domain with the negative outcome flagged here."}
{"term":"arrastar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_acquisition","concept":"sex_acquisition","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":35,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":77,"recognition_pct_peak":77,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To successfully pull or attract someone into a hookup; to 'drag' a target into a romantic-sexual encounter, emphasizing the active triumph of the seduction.","english_term":"to pull / to score / to drag someone home","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to drag/pull.' Implies the pursuer's effort and the target being drawn along. More emphatic about conquest than 'pegar'; the metaphor foregrounds the pursuer's agency."}
{"term":"fisgar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_acquisition","concept":"sex_acquisition","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":28,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":74,"recognition_pct_peak":74,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To hook someone romantically or sexually; to attract and land a partner through charm or calculated seduction, invoking the fishing metaphor of setting a hook.","english_term":"to hook / to reel in","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to hook' (as in fishing). Frames the target as a fish and the pursuer as an angler. More playful and strategic in connotation than 'arrastar'; implies patient technique over brute persistence."}
{"term":"dar em cima","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sexual_advance","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":25,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To hit on someone; to make direct romantic or sexual advances toward a person in a persistent or obvious manner.","english_term":"to hit on / to come on to","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Literally 'to give on top of.' The single most standard Brazilian expression for making advances. Universally understood across all generations, regions, and registers."}
{"term":"cantada","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"pickup_line","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":22,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A pickup line or flirtatious verbal approach; a charm offensive directed at someone to signal romantic or sexual interest.","english_term":"pickup line / come-on","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From 'cantar' (to sing), historically evoking a troubadour's serenade. A cantada can be a single witty opener or a sustained conversational approach. Not inherently crude; tone ranges from sweet to sleazy depending on content."}
{"term":"cantada pesada","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"aggressive_advance","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":52,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A heavy, forceful, or sexually overt pickup advance; a come-on that escalates beyond playful flirting into direct or pressuring sexual solicitation.","english_term":"heavy come-on / strong move","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Pesada' = heavy/intense. Frames the advance as more pressuring and sexual than a standard cantada; can border on harassment depending on context and delivery. The compound is descriptive rather than pejorative per se."}
{"term":"cantada safada","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"lewd_advance","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":63,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A dirty or sexually explicit pickup line; a come-on whose content is overtly vulgar, licentious, or lewd rather than merely forward.","english_term":"dirty come-on / lewd pickup line","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Safada' (fem. of safado) = dirty/naughty/perverted. Characterizes both the moral register of the approach and implicitly the character of its deliverer. More about explicit content than forcefulness — contrasts with cantada pesada which is about intensity."}
{"term":"papo de sedução","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"seduction_talk","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":86,"recognition_pct_peak":86,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Seduction talk; the verbal game or smooth conversational approach deployed to attract and seduce a potential partner.","english_term":"game / smooth talk / seduction patter","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Papo' = chat/talk; 'sedução' = seduction. Foregrounds the verbal and performative dimension of seduction rather than physical escalation. Sometimes used admiringly to describe someone with unusually effective social charisma."}
{"term":"paquera","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"flirting","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":12,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Flirting; playful, light romantic-sexual banter and mutual attention exchanged between two people who are attracted to each other, without overt pressure.","english_term":"flirting / a flirt","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"One of the most culturally central terms in Brazilian romantic vocabulary. Lighter and more reciprocal than a cantada; paquera implies mutual enjoyment rather than one-sided pressure. Also used as a noun for the flirting stage of a courtship."}
{"term":"paquerando","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"flirting","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":12,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":96,"recognition_pct_peak":96,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Actively flirting; present-participle form indicating someone is currently in the middle of a paquera exchange with another person.","english_term":"flirting with / hitting it off with","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Progressive form of 'paquerar.' 'Ele está paquerando a colega' = 'He's flirting with his colleague.' Slightly more dynamic and ongoing than the noun 'paquera'; the gerund marks the act as actively in progress."}
{"term":"flerte","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"flirting","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":12,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Flirting; a romantic-sexual verbal or behavioral exchange signaling attraction, borrowed directly from English.","english_term":"flirt / flirtation","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Direct loanword from English 'flirt/flirtation.' Slightly more deliberate or adult in register than 'paquera' and more common in print journalism and social media commentary on romantic dynamics. The loanword status gives it a mildly cosmopolitan or modern feel."}
{"term":"assanhado/assanhada","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexually_excited","concept":"sexual_flustered","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":35,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":91,"recognition_pct_peak":91,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexually worked up, frisky, or in a state of restless flirtatious arousal; describes someone who is visibly amorous, agitated, and eager for romantic or sexual attention.","english_term":"frisky / hot and bothered","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Gendered adjective (masc./fem. forms given). Literally relates to being ruffled or agitated, applied to humans and animals alike. The behavioral restlessness is as central as the arousal; it implies the person is acting on or displaying their excitement, not merely feeling it internally."}
{"term":"chegar junto","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"romantic_approach","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":18,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":83,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To make a move on someone; to approach a person with romantic or sexual intent, typically implying boldness or cooperative social effort.","english_term":"to make a move / to step to someone","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to come alongside/together.' Used both for an individual making a solo move and, in youth slang influenced by AAVE, for friends coordinating to help one of them hook up. Less aggressive in connotation than 'dar em cima'; implies smooth confidence rather than overt pressure."}
{"term":"chegar por baixo","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"indirect_seduction","concept":"sexual_advance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":22,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":79,"recognition_pct_peak":79,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To use a subtle, indirect, or flattering approach to seduce someone; to ease in romantically 'under the radar' through ingratiation rather than direct advance.","english_term":"to play it cool / to ease in / to butter someone up","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literally 'to come from below.' Contrasts strategically with a direct cantada: the pursuer uses compliments, small favors, and gradual escalation to lower the target's guard. Carries a mildly manipulative connotation — the indirectness is calculated, not shy."}
